    "problem_statement": "Add a virtual file system API call that triggers a proactive garbage collection of a mounted file system. A caller invokes fs_gc() on a mounted file system and it returns 0 on success. For the LittleFS backend, this should perform the underlying garbage-collection pass (an ignored request is not a failure), and the file system must remain mountable and unmountable cleanly before and after the call. The capability is gated behind a Kconfig option (CONFIG_FILE_SYSTEM_BACKEND-style CONFIG_FILE_SYSTEM_GC) that, when enabled, exposes the new function and the per-driver callback.",
